  "answer": "The assistant does not have a record of a specific sermon or lecture number or an exact section title for that material in “Systematic — Systematic Theology Vol2.” However, the teaching conveyed is that civil obligations are satisfied by payment of the debt regardless of who pays, because the creditor’s claim is on the amount owed, not on the debtor’s person. In contrast, criminal liability is personal; the offender himself must bear the penalty, and substitution is not permissible in human courts. Penal satisfaction differs from pecuniary satisfaction in that it does not automatically result in complete liberation, and the penalty need only be a just equivalent to the crime rather than a literal repayment of the injury."
